<LegalLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Which cookies Wrench Theory uses, why, and how to control them." updated="November 10, 2026">
  <p>Cookies are small text files stored by your browser. This page explains which cookies this site may use and how you can control them.</p>
  <h2>Types of cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Essential.</b> Needed for the site to work, for example to remember your consent choice.</li>
    <li><b>Analytics.</b> Help us understand which articles are read and how the site is used (for example Google Analytics).</li>
    <li><b>Advertising.</b> Set by Google and its partners to show and measure ads, and in some cases to personalize them.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve ads on this site. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
  <h2>Managing consent</h2>
  <p>Visitors in regions that require it are asked for consent before non-essential cookies are used. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the site will still work, but ads may be less relevant.</p>
  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when the tools we use change. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
</LegalLayout>
